      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To summarize the anesthesia managements on 63 CAD patients undergoing 1-stop hybrid revascularization from July 2007 to June 2009 in Fuwai Hospital."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "ECG, direct BP, SpO2, P(ET)CO2, CVP and body temperature were monitored during anesthesia. The management of intraoperative anesthesia should preferably use a small dosage of opioids with inhalation or intravenous anesthesia. At the same time, specific anticoagulation management was administered."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The hemodynamics were stabilized. the time of tracheal intubation were shorter. 6 patients were immediate extubated in the operating room with application of fast-track technology. No patient died."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Such minimally invasive surgery has little effect on the circulation. The difficulty of anesthetic management is smaller. Specific anticoagulation management is administered. Implementation of the Fast-track technology can demonstrate the further advantages in such surgery."
        }
      ]},
